@page "/docs/blazix-json"

<DocsPage Title="blazix.json" Description="Configuration for your project.">
    <p>The <code>blazix.json</code> file holds the configuration for your project.</p>
    <p>The CLI uses it to know where to put components, which namespace to give them, and what you&apos;ve installed.</p>
    <p><code>init</code> writes it, and <code>add</code> updates it. You can edit it by hand.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@ExampleCode" Language="json" Title="blazix.json" LineNumbers="true" />

    <DocsHeading Title="namespace" />
    <p>The namespace of your components. The registry&apos;s components are in <code>Blazix.Registry</code>, and <code>add</code> rewrites it to this one in every file it copies.</p>
    <p><code>init</code> makes it from your project&apos;s root namespace and the components folder.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@NamespaceCode" Language="json" Title="blazix.json" />

    <DocsHeading Title="componentsDir" />
    <p>Where <code>add</code> puts components, relative to the project. Set it with <code>init --dir</code>. Defaults to <code>Components/UI</code>. Each component gets a folder of its own in it, such as <code>Components/UI/Button</code>, and every folder shares <code>namespace</code>.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@DirCode" Language="json" Title="blazix.json" />

    <DocsHeading Title="version" />
    <p>The CLI version that set up the project. The components it copies are written against the <code>Blazix.Primitives</code> package of the same version.</p>

    <DocsHeading Title="rtl" />
    <p>Copy components right-to-left ready: <code>add</code> turns physical classes into logical ones (<code>ml-2</code> into <code>ms-2</code>, <code>left-0</code> into <code>start-0</code>) and flips directional icons under <code>rtl:</code>. Set it with <code>init --rtl</code> or <code>migrate rtl</code>. Defaults to <code>false</code>. See <a href="/docs/rtl">RTL</a>.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@RtlCode" Language="json" Title="blazix.json" />

    <DocsHeading Title="iconLibrary" />
    <p>The icon set the components draw their icons from: <code>lucide</code>, <code>tabler</code>, <code>hugeicons</code>, <code>phosphor</code>, <code>remixicon</code> or <code>fontawesome</code>. <code>add</code> and <code>init</code> install its package, such as <code>Blazix.Icons.Lucide</code>. Set it with <code>init --icon-library</code> or <code>migrate icons</code>. Defaults to <code>lucide</code>. See <a href="/docs/icons">Icons</a>.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@IconLibraryCode" Language="json" Title="blazix.json" />

    <DocsHeading Title="installed" />
    <p>What you&apos;ve added, with the version each came from. <code>list</code> marks these. To pick up a newer version of a component, run <code>add &lt;name&gt; --overwrite</code> and review the diff.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@InstalledCode" Language="json" Title="blazix.json" />
</DocsPage>

@code {
    private const string ExampleCode = """
        {
          "namespace": "MyApp.Components.UI",
          "componentsDir": "Components/UI",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "rtl": false,
          "iconLibrary": "lucide",
          "installed": {
            "utils": "0.1.0",
            "button": "0.1.0"
          }
        }
        """;

    private const string NamespaceCode = """
        {
          "namespace": "MyApp.Components.UI"
        }
        """;

    private const string DirCode = """
        {
          "componentsDir": "Components/UI"
        }
        """;

    private const string RtlCode = """
        {
          "rtl": true
        }
        """;

    private const string IconLibraryCode = """
        {
          "iconLibrary": "tabler"
        }
        """;

    private const string InstalledCode = """
        {
          "installed": {
            "utils": "0.1.0",
            "button": "0.1.0",
            "dropdown-menu": "0.1.0"
          }
        }
        """;
}
